[2026-03-15T08:50:25.020Z] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HEmKoJWCeS5GHKv9vWxejd","type":"tool_result","content":"# Replay MCP Skill File Content\n\nThis skill file describes **Replay MCP**, a tool for inspecting Replay.io recordings that \"perfectly capture everything that happened when a browser visited an app or other web page.\"\n\n## Key Components\n\n**Investigation Methodology:**\nThe document recommends a structured approach: frame questions, explore related events, explain findings, form hypotheses, and support conclusions with gathered data.\n\n**Exploratory Tools** help discover what happened:\n- Error detection (uncaught exceptions, React errors)\n- Timeline analysis (console messages, network requests, React renders)\n- Source code inspection (finding files, reading contents, searching patterns)\n\n**Explanatory Tools** clarify why events occurred:\n- Dependencies tracking (stack frames, control flow)\n- Details inspection (point descriptions, element properties, component trees, expressions)\n\n**Core Concept:**\n\"A specific point in the execution\" represents individual moments when JavaScript statements execute or significant events occur, while \"elements\" reference particular DOM nodes independent of time.\n\n**Practical Guidance:**\nThe file recommends using the Logpoint tool to track expression values across execution points and the ControlDependency tool to understand event sequencing and timing issues."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5e4cce03-c6a6-4315-b216-3d7fe11f1c2e","uuid":"90fe843a-514d-4d93-ae8b-0e540d24faf1","tool_use_result":{"bytes":4555,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# Replay MCP Skill File Content\n\nThis skill file describes **Replay MCP**, a tool for inspecting Replay.io recordings that \"perfectly capture everything that happened when a browser visited an app or other web page.\"\n\n## Key Components\n\n**Investigation Methodology:**\nThe document recommends a structured approach: frame questions, explore related events, explain findings, form hypotheses, and support conclusions with gathered data.\n\n**Exploratory Tools** help discover what happened:\n- Error detection (uncaught exceptions, React errors)\n- Timeline analysis (console messages, network requests, React renders)\n- Source code inspection (finding files, reading contents, searching patterns)\n\n**Explanatory Tools** clarify why events occurred:\n- Dependencies tracking (stack frames, control flow)\n- Details inspection (point descriptions, element properties, component trees, expressions)\n\n**Core Concept:**\n\"A specific point in the execution\" represents individual moments when JavaScript statements execute or significant events occur, while \"elements\" reference particular DOM nodes independent of time.\n\n**Practical Guidance:**\nThe file recommends using the Logpoint tool to track expression values across execution points and the ControlDependency tool to understand event sequencing and timing issues.","durationMs":3200,"url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/replayio/skills/refs/heads/main/skills/replay-mcp/SKILL.md"}}
[2026-03-15T08:50:25.722Z] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LnZaJCG3BuUUnekz1acKnH","type":"tool_result","content":"# Replay CLI Skill Reference\n\n## Overview\nReplay CLI is a tool for recording application sessions to gather performance data and debug issues. It supports recording, uploading, and managing recordings through command-line operations.\n\n## Installation\nInstall globally via npm, yarn, pnpm, or bun:\n```sh\nnpm i -g replayio\n```\n\n## Authentication\n1. Navigate to https://app.replay.io settings\n2. Create an API key\n3. Save it to the `REPLAY_API_KEY` environment variable\n\n## Key Commands\n\n**Recording & Upload:**\n- `replayio record [url]` - Launch browser and record a session\n- `replayio upload [ids...]` - Upload one or more recordings\n\n**Management:**\n- `replayio list [--json]` - View all local recordings\n- `replayio remove [ids...] [-a, --all]` - Delete recordings\n- `replayio login/logout` - Manage authentication\n\n**Utilities:**\n- `replayio info` - Display CLI and browser version info\n- `replayio update` - Update Replay Browser\n- `replayio upload-source-maps` - Upload source maps with various options\n\n## Workflow Example\nRecord a session at a specific URL, then upload it for viewing and debugging purposes. Use recording IDs from the list command to target specific uploads or removals.\n\n## MCP Server Integration\nInstall the Replay MCP Server in Claude for enhanced debugging capabilities using the `REPLAY_API_KEY` for authorization."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5e4cce03-c6a6-4315-b216-3d7fe11f1c2e","uuid":"97464729-779d-4e94-be79-1f75b396851f","tool_use_result":{"bytes":4854,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# Replay CLI Skill Reference\n\n## Overview\nReplay CLI is a tool for recording application sessions to gather performance data and debug issues. It supports recording, uploading, and managing recordings through command-line operations.\n\n## Installation\nInstall globally via npm, yarn, pnpm, or bun:\n```sh\nnpm i -g replayio\n```\n\n## Authentication\n1. Navigate to https://app.replay.io settings\n2. Create an API key\n3. Save it to the `REPLAY_API_KEY` environment variable\n\n## Key Commands\n\n**Recording & Upload:**\n- `replayio record [url]` - Launch browser and record a session\n- `replayio upload [ids...]` - Upload one or more recordings\n\n**Management:**\n- `replayio list [--json]` - View all local recordings\n- `replayio remove [ids...] [-a, --all]` - Delete recordings\n- `replayio login/logout` - Manage authentication\n\n**Utilities:**\n- `replayio info` - Display CLI and browser version info\n- `replayio update` - Update Replay Browser\n- `replayio upload-source-maps` - Upload source maps with various options\n\n## Workflow Example\nRecord a session at a specific URL, then upload it for viewing and debugging purposes. Use recording IDs from the list command to target specific uploads or removals.\n\n## MCP Server Integration\nInstall the Replay MCP Server in Claude for enhanced debugging capabilities using the `REPLAY_API_KEY` for authorization.","durationMs":4285,"url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/replayio/skills/refs/heads/main/skills/replay-cli/SKILL.md"}}
